cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these certificates, data or the verifier, please cite them as below."
type: dataset
title: "Certified m-independence of the first n zeros of the Riemann zeta function (n <= 700)"
authors:
  - family-names: Weisz
    given-names: Benjamin
repository-code: "https://github.com/wbeni95/zeta-zeros-linear-independence"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23652325"
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-25"
keywords:
  - Riemann zeta function
  - zeros of the zeta function
  - linear independence
  - lattice reduction
  - certified computation
abstract: >-
  Certificates that the first n nontrivial zeros of the Riemann zeta function admit no integer relation
  m_0 g_1 + ... + m_{n-1} g_n = 0 with 0 < max_{j>=1} |m_j| <= M, for n = 100, 200, 300, 400, 500 and 700
  (for n = 700, M = 257742). This improves Table 2 of Best and Trudgian (2015) by 6 to 8 orders of magnitude
  and extends it to n = 700. Includes the reduced lattice bases, the zero data and a ball-arithmetic verifier.
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Best
        given-names: D. G.
      - family-names: Trudgian
        given-names: T. S.
    title: "Linear relations of zeroes of the zeta-function"
    journal: "Mathematics of Computation"
    volume: 84
    issue: 294
    start: 2047
    end: 2058
    year: 2015
